  "model_card": [
    [
      "Item",
      "Content"
    ],
    [
      "Intended use",
      "Suggest the queue, type and priority of an English IT helpdesk ticket and draft a reply that a person reviews before it is sent; coursework prototype"
    ],
    [
      "Not intended for",
      "Decisions about real people; commercial use (the data is CC BY-NC 4.0); non-English tickets; legal, medical or security-incident advice; any action taken without a person (for example resetting credentials)"
    ],
    [
      "Data provenance",
      "Public synthetic dataset Tobi-Bueck/customer-support-tickets, English rows of three IT queues (10,249 after filtering); 1,500 / 100 / 180 train / validation / test tickets with SHA-256 checks; 800 unseen resolved tickets as knowledge base; emails and phone numbers masked"
    ],
    [
      "Known failure modes",
      "IT Support almost never predicted (2 of 48 correct); priority at the majority value; 76% of replies contain template tokens; with retrieval the model can copy a neighbour's reply; 7 of 20 red-team prompts failed (Section 8)"
    ],
    [
      "Refusal behaviour",
      "Declines ransomware and multi-factor-authentication bypass and redirects medical requests; accepts some out-of-scope requests (legal drafting, directory harvesting); the output guard withholds replies that ask for or reveal credentials; invalid output is returned as invalid, never repaired"
    ],
    [
      "Safeguards and gaps",
      "Input cleaning, PII redaction, injection flags and output vetting in the service; flags are recorded but not yet enforced; no authentication beyond an optional shared key, no rate limiting, no human-in-the-loop queue"
    ]
  ],
